Layer 2 — The Core Engine (Proprietary)

This license covers the protected "Core Engine" of the OSINT Sentinel
Workstation. The Core Engine includes:

  - Hardware Abstraction Layer (HAL)
    - WebGPU compute kernels (WGSL shaders)
    - Worker thread pool and worker scripts
    - Streaming I/O pipelines
    - WebCodecs integration
    - WASM SIMD kernels
    - CUDA native bridges
  - Hydrology engine internals (Priority-Flood, runoff simulation)
  - Canopy engine internals
  - Prediction engine (severe-weather, storm-track, radar nowcast,
    sensor-failure, ocean-atmosphere coupler)
  - Native bridges (OpenXR, CUDA, AVX2/AVX-512, NVENC)
  - Heavy compute kernels (DEM slope, hillshade, anomaly, band math)
  - GPU kernel compilation and dispatch
  - Multi-node synchronization
  - HyperForge integration transport

GRANT OF LICENSE
----------------

1. Evaluation and Trial Use
   Visentrix grants you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable,
   revocable license to use the Core Engine in evaluation mode for a
   period of fourteen (14) days from first installation, subject to the
   terms of this license.

2. Licensed Use
   Upon purchase of a valid Visentrix license key, Visentrix grants you
   a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to use the Core
   Engine on a single machine, bound to that machine's hardware
   fingerprint, for the duration of the license term.

3. Open Cockpit Integration
   The Core Engine may be used in conjunction with the Visentrix Open
   Cockpit (Layer 1) software. The Cockpit may operate independently
   without the Core Engine, with reduced functionality.

